---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PolicySection from "../../components/Privacy/PolicySection.astro";

const lastUpdated = "November 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Rhymate privacy — digitowly"
  description="How Rhymate handles your data. No accounts, no analytics, no ads. Your lyrics stay on your devices."
  tone="mint"
>
  <section class="gutter relative overflow-hidden bg-mint pt-36 pb-16 text-pine sm:pt-44 sm:pb-24">
    <div
      aria-hidden="true"
      class="pointer-events-none absolute -top-[25vw] -right-[30vw] size-[70vw] rounded-full bg-[#91ffe2]/70 blur-3xl"
    ></div>
    <p class="rise relative text-sm font-medium tracking-[0.2em] text-teal uppercase">
      <a href="/rhymate" class="hover:underline">Rhymate</a> · Privacy
    </p>
    <h1
      class="display rise relative mt-6 text-huge text-balance"
      style="animation-delay: 120ms"
    >
      Your lyrics{" "}
      <span class="serif-accent tracking-normal text-teal">stay yours.</span>
    </h1>
    <p
      class="rise relative mt-10 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-pine/80"
      style="animation-delay: 260ms"
    >
      No accounts, no analytics, no ads. We don’t run a server that collects
      anything from the app. Here’s the little that does happen with data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="gutter bg-paper py-20 sm:py-32">
    <div class="mb-6 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-end sm:justify-between">
      <h2 class="display text-big">The details</h2>
      <p class="serif-accent text-xl text-ink/60">
        Last updated {lastUpdated}.
      </p>
    </div>

    <PolicySection no="01" title="Who is responsible">
      <p>
        Rhymate is made by <strong>digitowly</strong> · Robert Pasdziernik,
        Düsseldorfer Straße 159, 51063 Köln, Germany,{" "}
        <a href="mailto:info@digitowly.com">info@digitowly.com</a>. More details
        are in the <a href="/impressum">Impressum</a>.
      </p>
    </PolicySection>

    <PolicySection no="02" title="Your songs & favourites">
      <p>
        Your lyrics, chords and favourites are stored on your device. If you use
        iCloud, they sync through your private iCloud database at Apple. We
        can’t see that data, and neither can anyone else except you (and Apple,
        under their{" "}
        <a
          href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          privacy policy
        </a>
        ).
      </p>
    </PolicySection>

    <PolicySection no="03" title="Rhymes & definitions">
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Rhyme and synonym searches.</strong> When you look up a word,
          that word is sent to the{" "}
          <a
            href="https://www.datamuse.com/api/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Datamuse API
          </a>{" "}
          to find matches. Only the word is sent, never your lyrics.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Definitions.</strong> When you open a word’s definition, that
          word is sent to{" "}
          <a
            href="https://en.wiktionary.org/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Wiktionary
          </a>
          , run by the Wikimedia Foundation (
          <a
            href="https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Policy:Privacy_policy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            privacy policy
          </a>
          ).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        As with any internet request, these services receive your IP address
        technically. Both are based in the USA. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b)
        GDPR: without sending the word, we can’t find rhymes for it. (We tried
        guessing. Results were poor.)
      </p>
    </PolicySection>

    <PolicySection no="04" title="Your rights">
      <p>
        Your rights under the GDPR, and who to complain to, are listed on our{" "}
        <a href="/privacy">main privacy page</a>. Since we don’t hold any of
        your Rhymate data, deleting the app (and its iCloud data) deletes
        everything.
      </p>
    </PolicySection>

    <PolicySection no="05" title="Changes">
      <p>
        If a new Rhymate feature changes how data is handled, we’ll update this
        page first.
      </p>
    </PolicySection>
  </section>
</Layout>
